<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tito Venier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1363</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a> Venier was a Venetian noble of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> who in 1363 led the revolt of the island's Venetian colonists against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, sparked by a new tax for the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a>. The rebels proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-saint">Saint Titus</a>, named after the island's patron saint, and sought Greek support. Venice crushed the revolt in 1364 and executed its leaders.</p></div>
